      "text": "To find the area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle given its base and height. However, this problem can be solved using the determinant method for the area of a triangle with coordinates \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\((x_1, y_1) = (0, 0)\\), \\((x_2, y_2) = (0, 5)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3) = (7, 12)\\) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0(5 - 12) + 0(12 - 0) + 7(0 - 5) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSimplifying inside the absolute value:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + 0 + 7(-5) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -35 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 35 = 17.5\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the triangle is \\(17.5\\) square units.\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Function to calculate the area of a triangle given its vertices\ndef triangle_area(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3):\n    return 0.5 * abs(x1*(y2 - y3) + x2*(y3 - y1) + x3*(y1 - y2))\n\n# Coordinates of the vertices\nx1, y1 = 0, 0\nx2, y2 = 0, 5\nx3, y3 = 7, 12\n\n# Calculate the area\narea = triangle_area(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3)\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n17.5\n```\nThe area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\) is \\(\\boxed{17.5}\\) square units.",
