      "text": "The area of a triangle with vertices at $(x_1, y_1)$, $(x_2, y_2)$, and $(x_3, y_3)$ can be found using the formula:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Area} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\n\\end{align*}\nPlugging in the coordinates $(0,0)$, $(0,5)$, and $(7,12)$, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Area} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0(5 - 12) + 0(12 - 0) + 7(0 - 5) \\right| \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -35 \\right| \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{17.5}\n\\end{align*}\nThe answer is: 17.5",
